Chapter: GptArrayGeomGuardTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Gpt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The negative control for gpt-array-geom-ok. The .disk sidecar is the valid gop-fat16
 image with ONE change: NumberOfPartitionEntries at header offset 80 is 100000. That count is the array CRC's OWN EXTENT, so it has to be refused BEFORE any CRC is trusted -- a corrupt count moves the window and a reader then computes a perfectly valid CRC over the wrong bytes. The header CRC is RECOMPUTED in the fixture so it still verifies, which is what forces the refusal to come from the geometry test and not from stage 9.

 Ablate gpt-array-geom-ok and this flips to esp-start=64: the array would run past FirstUsableLBA and 100000 entries do not fit the medium, and the table is
 accepted anyway.

Section: Main

  show-esp : [Device.Port] Text
  show-esp = act
    s <- gpt-esp-start
    "esp-start=" & show s & " stage=" & show (xdiag-get gfat-cell-stage)
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    a <- show-esp
    print-line-uni a
  end